In order to prove the offences punishable under section 279 IPC, the prosecution has to prove beyond reasonable doubt, the following mandatory ingredients:
 That accident actually took place;
 That a vehicle was driven or ridden by the accused at the time of accident;  That the accused was driving it on a public way; and  The said vehicle was driven in a rash or negligent manner;
14.

